DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The bbtthhiidddd daemon handles remote Bluetooth HID devices.

     The options are as follows:

     --aa _B_D___A_D_D_R
             Specify the local address to listen on.  By default, the server
             will listen on ANY address.  The address can be specified as
             BD_ADDR or name.  If a name was specified, the bbtthhiidddd daemon will
             attempt to resolve the name via bt_gethostbyname(3).

     --cc _f_i_l_e
             Specify path to the configuration file.  The default path is
             _/_e_t_c_/_b_l_u_e_t_o_o_t_h_/_b_t_h_i_d_d_._c_o_n_f.

     --dd      Do not detach from the controlling terminal, i.e., run in fore‐
             ground.

     --HH _f_i_l_e
             Specify path to the known HIDs file.  The default path is
             _/_v_a_r_/_d_b_/_b_t_h_i_d_d_._h_i_d_s.

     --hh      Display usage message and exit.

     --pp _f_i_l_e
             Specify path to the PID file.  The default path is
             _/_v_a_r_/_r_u_n_/_b_t_h_i_d_d_._p_i_d.

     --tt _v_a_l  Specify client rescan interval in seconds.  The bbtthhiidddd daemon
             will periodically scan for newly configured Bluetooth HID devices
             or disconnected “passive” Bluetooth HID devices and will attempt
             to establish an outgoing connection.  The default rescan interval
             is 10 seconds.

     --uu      Enable support for input event device protocol.  Requires evdev
             and uinput drivers to be loaded with kldload(8) or compiled into
             the kernel.

